","type":"text"},{"text":"per component, each copy of a parallel edge counting as its own edge. Self-loops are never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taken. The forest depends only on the generator’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sequence, so a seeded generator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reproduces it on every platform.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m) plus the walks: the mean hitting time of the root, expected, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n m) at worst and far less on well-connected graphs.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/randomspanningtree(using:)"]}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/SpanningForest":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A spanning forest of an undirected graph: one spanning tree per connected component, as edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions in the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", with the sum of their weights."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/spanningforest","type":"topic","title":"SpanningForest","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SpanningTrees","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/randomSpanningTree(us